<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Union Island is one of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grenadines">Grenadines</a>, part of Saint Vincent and the Grenadines, with its main village at Clifton. In December 1979, weeks after independence, a brief armed uprising there was put down with help from Barbados. In July 2024 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-beryl">Hurricane Beryl</a> destroyed or damaged most of its buildings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/union-island.jpg" alt="Union Island" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Acp · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unionisland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
